-895f-17d752e723fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0db6d573366a6fc6e07a50fb2308a2ded8d53ea35bd2030d19892695cd81a49d","event_uuid":"ec3910a8-9243-41cd-9ed9-b5b25f4274bb","position":{"commit_sha":"15cfd37800985f662290b6fea9b004aea4871bfb","position":"1788389645715996941-ec3910a8-9243-41cd-9ed9-b5b25f4274bb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e524ac026fad23b2a227d28116b25886d3de34f0df72689719d4bc50130b71c0","event_uuid":"f115a605-bf01-471d-a360-170ca5be4917","position":{"commit_sha":"15cfd37800985f662290b6fea9b004aea4871bfb","position":"1788389645768097275-f115a605-bf01-471d-a360-170ca5be4917"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1783289317878533001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1441bbd0-0ec2-419a-aa79-7b1959b3cda5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9f78-ccbf-9248-4097"},{"link_uuid":"147b953f-dd4a-4c10-83b6-6e0cb816098b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877"},{"link_uuid":"0607f587-f706-4cf4-b579-f88cfbac900f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPlan-review criterion prompts ship with no behavioral regression oracle. Of the 50\nplan-review criteria returned by `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`,\nonly 12 have an eval spec across `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and `.rebar/evals/`. A\ncontributor editing any of the other rubrics under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` learns\nnothing if the edit reintroduces a false positive or drops a catch. ADR 0109 delivered a way\nto MEASURE a proposed change (the three-tier replay harness); it did not deliver an assertion\nof any criterion's required behavior on concrete material.\n\nThe material already exists. The committed manifest\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-2026-08-30.manifest.json` records 6,482\nsidecar rows (`verified_ratio` 0.9568), and\n`plan_replay/corpus.py` reconstructs each row's at-review plan text. `plan_review/sidecar.py`\nretains, per finding, the `criteria` list, `cohort` (`sidecar.py:667-672`), `norm_id`,\n`decision`, and `decision_margin` — enough to state, for a real plan, which criteria fired,\nand — via the per-finding `cohort` set — which criteria were routed yet stayed silent.\n\n## Approach\n\nMine that corpus offline into per-criterion fire/no-fire eval fixtures on real plans, and\nadmit a fixture only after it reproduces against current code.\n\n**No-fire evidence predicate.** The sidecar persists only findings that FIRED, so silence is\nan ABSENCE inference, never on its own a valid `expect: pass` case: silence from the criterion\nnever being routed to that plan is indistinguishable from silence from finding nothing. The\nselector admits a plan as no-fire evidence for criterion C only when C appears in the `cohort`\nset of some finding recorded for that plan (`sidecar.py:667-672`, proving C was routed) AND no\nfinding on that plan cites C; a row with a MISSING `cohort` key is treated as unknown and\nskipped, never emitted as `expect: pass` (the sidecar contract: missing cohort is unknown,\nnever an empty set). No-fire reproduction consensus ranges over the equal-`material_fingerprint`\nreviews meeting this predicate; the selector owns it, the emitter transcribes it.\n\n**Only inline-runnable criteria are mined.** `eval_solver.py:100-140` has three runner\npaths: generic criteria run over inline plan text, `CONTAINER_CRITERIA` (G3/G4/decomp-shape)\nrequire a `children` payload, and ISF RAISES on any inline fixture. Both non-inline classes\nstill carry a `cohort` tag, so the selector EXCLUDES them from inline mining and the\nself-healing loop files an `unreliable-criterion:` ticket (reason: finder not inline-runnable)\nfor each; the admission runner treats a fixture whose finder rejects its shape as\nWITHHELD-with-reason, never a hard error.\n\nThis fits because the fixture is what the existing machinery already consumes:\n`rebar criteria eval` runs a criterion's cases through its real Pass-1 finder\n(`eval_solver.py:139-142`) via the validated `.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` seam\n(`eval.py:69-78`). A fixture adds zero production tokens, cannot\nbias a live review, and composes with the ADR 0109 harness rather than duplicating it.\n\nThis epic REPLACES its earlier R-4 framing (examples injected into reviewer prompts): the\nPass-1 rubric is assembled into `instructions` AFTER the cache breakpoint\n(`pass1.py:283-298`), so prompt-resident examples re-bill on every chunk forever, and a false\npositive used as both prompt example and eval case makes the eval measure nothing.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Injecting anything into reviewer prompts. No file under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`\n  changes in this epic.\n- Fixtures for criteria that already have a spec. `eval.py:69-78` resolves a project spec\n  as a REPLACEMENT for the packaged one, so writing one there would delete the packaged\n  cases.\n- Shipping rebar's fixtures as packaged core for other projects. The tooling is the reusable\n  artifact; a project overriding criteria owns its own evals, as it already owns its tests.\n- Closing the drift the admission run discovers. Each entry becomes a follow-on ticket\n  linked `discovered_from` this epic.\n- Per-finding true/false-positive labelling or human adjudication (the 2026-07-16 attempt\n  was invalidated at ~79% contaminated labels,\n  `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/README.md:112-118`; not retried here).\n- Restructuring the prompt cache so eval prefixes become cacheable.\n\n## Budget\n\nEpic ceiling **$450** including a $75 reserve, enforced by the parameterized ledger and\nallocated per child: ledger $0, selector $0, emitter $0, admission runner $250,\nchange-triggered execution $25, self-healing loop $100, ADR/docs $0. The admission bootstrap\ncentral estimate is $112 (band $68-$229) at the per-call rates in\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl`. Steady-state cost after this epic\nis zero unless a rubric changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A no-fire (`expect: pass`) case for criterion C is emitted only when C is in the\n      `cohort` set of some finding on that plan AND no finding on that plan cites C; a row\n      with a missing `cohort` key is skipped, never emitted; verified by `pytest` over a\n      synthetic corpus with an in-cohort silent plan (emitted), a never-in-cohort plan\n      (skipped), a missing-cohort row (skipped), and a container/ISF-class criterion\n      (excluded from inline mining).\n- [ ] Every plan-review criterion that `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`\n      reports and that had no eval spec when this epic opened either has a spec file under\n      `.rebar/evals/`, or an open ticket titled `unreliable-criterion: <criterion-id>`\n      recording why it has none; verified by a script that sets the routing key set against\n      `ls .rebar/evals/ src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and the open-ticket titles, and exits\n      non-zero if any criterion is in neither set.\n- [ ] No fixture enters `.rebar/evals/` without having reproduced against current code, and\n      the candidates that failed to reproduce are recorded with both their historical and\n      observed behavior; verified by the committed drift report plus the admission run's\n      admitted/withheld counts.\n- [ ] A criterion's fixtures execute when that criterion's rubric file changes, and the\n      criteria covered by this epic do not join the existing weekly live sweep; verified by\n      `grep` of the resolved weekly spec list showing none of the new prompt ids.\n- [ ] A run whose pre-flight estimate would exceed the epic ceiling is refused before it\n      issues any model call; verified by `pytest` over the ledger refusal test.\n- [ ] No file under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` is modified by this epic; verified by\n      `git diff --stat origin/main..HEAD -- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` producing no output.\n- [ ] The mining and admission protocol is recorded as an ADR under `docs/adr/` and\n      referenced from `docs/plan-review-gate.md`; verified by `grep -q` for the ADR filename\n      in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Child decomposition\n\nEach acceptance criterion above is owned by at least one child, non-overlapping:\n\n- No-fire predicate AC -> the selector (owns/applies the cohort + no-finding predicate) and\n  the emitter (transcribes no-fire candidates to `expect: pass`).\n- Coverage AC -> the selector (trustworthy candidates), the emitter (validated specs) and\n  the admission runner (writes survivors); residual gaps + container/ISF criteria -> the\n  self-healing loop, which files the `unreliable-criterion:` tickets.\n- Reproduction/drift AC -> the admission runner.\n- Change-triggered execution AC -> the change-triggered execution child.\n- Budget-refusal AC -> the ledger parameterization child, consumed by the admission runner.\n- Untouched-prompts AC -> a constraint on every child; no child edits a rubric.\n- ADR AC -> the ADR and docs child.\n\nOrdering: selector -> emitter; emitter + ledger -> admission runner; admission runner ->\nchange-triggered execution + self-healing loop; ADR/docs lands last.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"],["relates_to","9f78-ccbf-9248-4097"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ec3910a8-9243-41cd-9ed9-b5b25f4274bb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["plan-review","dso-gap","r-4","calibration","evals","fixtures","regression-oracle"],"ticket_id":"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Plan-review per-criterion regression fixtures mined from the review sidecar record (R-4)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["147b953f-dd4a-4c10-83b6-6e0cb816098b","d72394ff-8606-4ccf-951f-851dcc88b033","2f359819-87ef-4507-a08f-27643300b8f1","efc950f6-6b69-45c7-8b2b-8ff337245efa","0607f587-f706-4cf4-b579-f88cfbac900f","5f8f43d5-f442-4168-bf29-b397197ee070","a74b5cd0-dbc6-415f-99ae-6b06b7b4d416","263d2c4e-e795-4311-a2a3-9e4a722ba9fd","037a38c1-694e-428b-895f-17d752e723fd","ec3910a8-9243-41cd-9ed9-b5b25f4274bb","f115a605-bf01-471d-a360-170ca5be4917"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788391760139981001,"uuid":"73581362-248b-4456-9883-51d24c78c5a9"}